                <pb facs="0383" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.956/37</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-09T19:00:00-05:00">November 9, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>346. Reference Allison’s Nov. 8, 2 p.m., from Tsingtao. Provided you consider it
                    advisable, the Department has no objection to Allison’s <pb facs="0384" n="376"
                        xml:id="pg376"/> remaining temporarily at Tsinan to handle any urgent and
                    important matters which require attention, but feels that he should, upon the
                    completion of emergency duties, return to Nanking to report and to discuss with
                    you the subject matter of the telegram under reference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
